{
  "name": "m4-noise-scala",
  "description": [
    "Calibration, no code change: every variant is the same build, `c84dea8aa7`. How much of the fork-to-fork spread on the scala corpus comes from short warmup and from background JIT timing? Read each variant's spread across forks, not the difference in their means.",
    "",
    "`wi4` is the setup most current campaigns use. `wi12` warms for 12 compiles. `xbatch` adds `-Xbatch`, so compilation blocks the thread that asked for it and changes timing, so only its spread is meaningful, not its time. `jit8` sets `-XX:CICompilerCount=8` to warm up faster at the same 4 warmup compiles; compare both its spread and whether its iterations plateau sooner."
  ],
  "variants": {
    "wi4": "",
    "wi12": "",
    "xbatch": "-Xbatch",
    "jit8": "-XX:CICompilerCount=8"
  },
  "variantJmhArgs": {
    "wi4": "-wi 4",
    "wi12": "-wi 12",
    "xbatch": "-wi 4",
    "jit8": "-wi 4"
  },
  "builds": {
    "wi4": {
      "checkout": "/Users/jzaugg-virtus/code/.worktrees/scala/analyzer-11367-base",
      "env": {
        "SCALA_CHECKOUT": "{checkout}",
        "SCALA_RELEASE_OPT": "1"
      }
    },
